mastery.question_text:
Construct a spanning tree of this network. Crossing edges meet only where a vertex is marked.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2);
\coordinate (B) at (2,3);
\coordinate (C) at (4,3);
\coordinate (D) at (6,2);
\coordinate (E) at (6,0);
\coordinate (F) at (4,-1);
\coordinate (G) at (2,-1);
\coordinate (H) at (0,0);
\draw (A) -- (B) -- (C) -- (D) -- (E) -- (F) -- (G) -- (H) -- (A);
\draw (B) -- (H);
\draw (C) -- (F);
\draw (B) -- (F);
\draw (C) -- (G);
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$D$};
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$E$};
\fill (F) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$F$};
\fill (G) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$G$};
\fill (H) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$H$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Construct a spanning tree of this network, which includes a loop at $A$ and two edges between $B$ and $C$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,1);
\coordinate (B) at (1.5,3);
\coordinate (C) at (4,3);
\coordinate (D) at (5.5,1);
\coordinate (E) at (4,0);
\coordinate (F) at (1.5,0);
\coordinate (G) at (2.75,1.5);
\draw (A) -- (B) -- (C) -- (D) -- (E) -- (F) -- (A);
\draw (A) .. controls (-1.5,2.5) and (-1.5,-0.5) .. (A);
\draw (B) to[bend left=30] (C);
\draw (A) -- (G);
\draw (B) -- (G);
\draw (C) -- (G);
\draw (D) -- (G);
\draw (E) -- (G);
\draw (F) -- (G);
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[below left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[above right] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$D$};
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$E$};
\fill (F) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$F$};
\fill (G) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$G$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
